    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d149-a1">

                <pb facs="0214" n="206" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg206"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Under Secretary to the Government of India</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Pringle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        American Consul General at Calcutta</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 350 (44)–(I. T. C.)/41</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Simla</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-06-25">25 June, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your letter No. 660 dated
                    the 7th May 1941,<anchor n="50" xml:id="d149-f1"/> I am directed to say that,
                    having regard to the special circumstances of the case, the Government of India
                    have been pleased to sanction the issue of special licences for such goods as
                    may be imported by American Missionary Societies, and philanthropic
                    institutions, and are free gifts from the United States of America and which,
                    therefore, involve no transfer of foreign exchange. The licences will
                    accordingly be marked “Custom Licence: Not valid for transfer of foreign
                    exchange”.</p>
                <pb facs="0215" n="207" xml:id="pg207"/>
                <p>2. Necessary instructions are being issued to the Import Trade Controllers and
                    the organizations in question may be instructed to apply for the licences, when
                    required, to the Import Trade Controller concerned giving full details (e. g.
                    description, value, etc.) of each importation.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>R. J. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Pringle</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
